<title>PERU: TABLE - Peru's H1 wheat output falls 21 percent.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Peru's H1 wheat output falls 21 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table outlines Peru's</p>
<p>latest wheat production and import figures released Friday:</p>
<p>		    PRODUCTION	    IMPORTS</p>
<p> June 1996	50,600 tonnes	 52,100 tonnes</p>
<p> June 1997	41,900 tonnes	 74,300 tonnes</p>
<p> Jan-June 1996  63,400 million tonnes   498,000 tonnes</p>
<p>Jan-June 1997  50,200 million tonnest  547,000 tonnes</p>
<p>NOTES:</p>
<p>- Source for statistics is Peru's Agriculture Ministry.</p>
<p>- Peru's wheat is grown mostly in the central and southeastern Andean regions.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
